---Specifies a scheduled task used to back up a selection of resources.
---@class aws.backup.BackupRule
---@field RuleName aws.backup.BackupRuleName A display name for a backup rule. Must contain 1 to 50 alphanumeric or '-_.' characters.
---@field TargetBackupVaultName aws.backup.BackupVaultName The name of a logical container where backups are stored. Backup vaults are identified by names that are unique to the account used to create them and the Amazon Web Services Region where they are created.
---@field TargetLogicallyAirGappedBackupVaultArn? aws.backup.ARN The ARN of a logically air-gapped vault. ARN must be in the same account and Region. If provided, supported fully managed resources back up directly to logically air-gapped vault, while other supported resources create a temporary (billable) snapshot in backup vault, then copy it to logically air-gapped vault. Unsupported resources only back up to the specified backup vault.
---@field ScheduleExpression? aws.backup.CronExpression A cron expression in UTC specifying when Backup initiates a backup job. When no CRON expression is provided, Backup will use the default expression cron(0 5 ? * * *).
---@field StartWindowMinutes? aws.backup.WindowMinutes A value in minutes after a backup is scheduled before a job will be canceled if it doesn't start successfully. This value is optional. If this value is included, it must be at least 60 minutes to avoid errors.
---@field CompletionWindowMinutes? aws.backup.WindowMinutes A value in minutes after a backup job is successfully started before it must be completed or it will be canceled by Backup. This value is optional.
---@field Lifecycle? aws.backup.Lifecycle The lifecycle defines when a protected resource is transitioned to cold storage and when it expires. Backup transitions and expires backups automatically according to the lifecycle that you define.
---@field RecoveryPointTags? distilled.Secret The tags that are assigned to resources that are associated with this rule when restored from backup.
---@field RuleId? aws.backup.string Uniquely identifies a rule that is used to schedule the backup of a selection of resources.
---@field CopyActions? aws.backup.CopyActions An array of CopyAction objects, which contains the details of the copy operation.
---@field EnableContinuousBackup? aws.backup.Boolean Specifies whether Backup creates continuous backups. True causes Backup to create continuous backups capable of point-in-time restore (PITR). False (or not specified) causes Backup to create snapshot backups.
---@field ScheduleExpressionTimezone? aws.backup.Timezone The timezone in which the schedule expression is set. By default, ScheduleExpressions are in UTC. You can modify this to a specified timezone.
---@field IndexActions? aws.backup.IndexActions IndexActions is an array you use to specify how backup data should be indexed.
---@field ScanActions? aws.backup.ScanActions Contains your scanning configuration for the backup rule and includes the malware scanner, and scan mode of either full or incremental.

