---@field ConditionKey aws.backup.ConditionKey The key in a key-value pair. For example, in the tag Department: Accounting, Department is the key.
---@field ConditionValue aws.backup.ConditionValue The value in a key-value pair. For example, in the tag Department: Accounting, Accounting is the value.

---@alias aws.backup.ConditionKey string

---Includes information about tags you define to assign tagged resources to a backup plan.
---@class aws.backup.ConditionParameter
---@field ConditionKey? aws.backup.ConditionKey The key in a key-value pair. For example, in the tag Department: Accounting, Department is the key.
---@field ConditionValue? aws.backup.ConditionValue The value in a key-value pair. For example, in the tag Department: Accounting, Accounting is the value.

---@alias aws.backup.ConditionParameters aws.backup.ConditionParameter[]

---@alias aws.backup.ConditionType "STRINGEQUALS"

---@alias aws.backup.ConditionValue string

---Contains information about which resources to include or exclude from a backup plan using their tags. Conditions are case sensitive.
---@class aws.backup.Conditions
---@field StringEquals? aws.backup.ConditionParameters Filters the values of your tagged resources for only those resources that you tagged with the same value. Also called "exact matching."
---@field StringNotEquals? aws.backup.ConditionParameters Filters the values of your tagged resources for only those resources that you tagged that do not have the same value. Also called "negated matching."
---@field StringLike? aws.backup.ConditionParameters Filters the values of your tagged resources for matching tag values with the use of a wildcard character (*) anywhere in the string. For example, "prod*" or "*rod*" matches the tag value "production".
---@field StringNotLike? aws.backup.ConditionParameters Filters the values of your tagged resources for non-matching tag values with the use of a wildcard character (*) anywhere in the string.

---Backup can't perform the action that you requested until it finishes performing a previous action. Try again later.
---@class aws.backup.ConflictException
---@field Code? aws.backup.string
---@field Message? aws.backup.string
---@field Type? aws.backup.string
---@field Context? aws.backup.string

---The parameters for a control. A control can have zero, one, or more than one parameter. An example of a control with two parameters is: "backup plan frequency is at least daily and the retention period is at least 1 year". The first parameter is daily. The second parameter is 1 year.
---@class aws.backup.ControlInputParameter
---@field ParameterName? aws.backup.ParameterName The name of a parameter, for example, BackupPlanFrequency.
---@field ParameterValue? aws.backup.ParameterValue The value of parameter, for example, hourly.

---@alias aws.backup.ControlInputParameters aws.backup.ControlInputParameter[]

---@alias aws.backup.ControlName string

---A framework consists of one or more controls. Each control has its own control scope. The control scope can include one or more resource types, a combination of a tag key and value, or a combination of one resource type and one resource ID. If no scope is specified, evaluations for the rule are triggered when any resource in your recording group changes in configuration.
---@class aws.backup.ControlScope
---@field ComplianceResourceIds? aws.backup.ComplianceResourceIdList The ID of the only Amazon Web Services resource that you want your control scope to contain.
---@field ComplianceResourceTypes? aws.backup.ResourceTypeList Describes whether the control scope includes one or more types of resources, such as EFS or RDS.
---@field Tags? aws.backup.stringMap The tag key-value pair applied to those Amazon Web Services resources that you want to trigger an evaluation for a rule. A maximum of one key-value pair can be provided. The tag value is optional, but it cannot be an empty string if you are creating or editing a framework from the console (though the value can be an empty string when included in a CloudFormation template).

