---Contains detailed information about the recovery points stored in a backup vault.
---@class aws.backup.RecoveryPointByBackupVault
---@field RecoveryPointArn? aws.backup.ARN An Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that uniquely identifies a recovery point; for example, arn:aws:backup:us-east-1:123456789012:recovery-point:1EB3B5E7-9EB0-435A-A80B-108B488B0D45.
---@field BackupVaultName? aws.backup.BackupVaultName The name of a logical container where backups are stored. Backup vaults are identified by names that are unique to the account used to create them and the Amazon Web Services Region where they are created.
---@field BackupVaultArn? aws.backup.ARN An ARN that uniquely identifies a backup vault; for example, arn:aws:backup:us-east-1:123456789012:backup-vault:aBackupVault.
---@field SourceBackupVaultArn? aws.backup.ARN The backup vault where the recovery point was originally copied from. If the recovery point is restored to the same account this value will be null.
---@field ResourceArn? aws.backup.ARN An ARN that uniquely identifies a resource. The format of the ARN depends on the resource type.
---@field ResourceType? aws.backup.ResourceType The type of Amazon Web Services resource saved as a recovery point; for example, an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume or an Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) database. For Windows Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS) backups, the only supported resource type is Amazon EC2.
---@field CreatedBy? aws.backup.RecoveryPointCreator Contains identifying information about the creation of a recovery point, including the BackupPlanArn, BackupPlanId, BackupPlanVersion, and BackupRuleId of the backup plan that is used to create it.
---@field IamRoleArn? aws.backup.IAMRoleArn Specifies the IAM role ARN used to create the target recovery point; for example, arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/S3Access.
---@field Status? aws.backup.RecoveryPointStatus A status code specifying the state of the recovery point.
---@field StatusMessage? aws.backup.string A message explaining the current status of the recovery point.
---@field CreationDate? aws.backup.timestamp The date and time a recovery point is created, in Unix format and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). The value of CreationDate is accurate to milliseconds. For example, the value 1516925490.087 represents Friday, January 26, 2018 12:11:30.087 AM.
---@field InitiationDate? aws.backup.timestamp The date and time when the backup job that created this recovery point was initiated, in Unix format and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
---@field CompletionDate? aws.backup.timestamp The date and time a job to restore a recovery point is completed, in Unix format and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). The value of CompletionDate is accurate to milliseconds. For example, the value 1516925490.087 represents Friday, January 26, 2018 12:11:30.087 AM.
---@field BackupSizeInBytes? aws.backup.Long The size, in bytes, of a backup.
---@field CalculatedLifecycle? aws.backup.CalculatedLifecycle A CalculatedLifecycle object containing DeleteAt and MoveToColdStorageAt timestamps.
---@field Lifecycle? aws.backup.Lifecycle The lifecycle defines when a protected resource is transitioned to cold storage and when it expires. Backup transitions and expires backups automatically according to the lifecycle that you define.
---@field EncryptionKeyArn? aws.backup.ARN The server-side encryption key that is used to protect your backups; for example, arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:111122223333:key/1234abcd-12ab-34cd-56ef-1234567890ab.
---@field IsEncrypted aws.backup.Boolean2 A Boolean value that is returned as TRUE if the specified recovery point is encrypted, or FALSE if the recovery point is not encrypted.
---@field LastRestoreTime? aws.backup.timestamp The date and time a recovery point was last restored, in Unix format and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). The value of LastRestoreTime is accurate to milliseconds. For example, the value 1516925490.087 represents Friday, January 26, 2018 12:11:30.087 AM.
---@field ParentRecoveryPointArn? aws.backup.ARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the parent (composite) recovery point.
---@field CompositeMemberIdentifier? aws.backup.string The identifier of a resource within a composite group, such as nested (child) recovery point belonging to a composite (parent) stack. The ID is transferred from the logical ID within a stack.
---@field IsParent aws.backup.Boolean2 This is a boolean value indicating this is a parent (composite) recovery point.
---@field ResourceName? aws.backup.string The non-unique name of the resource that belongs to the specified backup.
---@field VaultType? aws.backup.VaultType The type of vault in which the described recovery point is stored.
---@field IndexStatus? aws.backup.IndexStatus This is the current status for the backup index associated with the specified recovery point.
---@field IndexStatusMessage? aws.backup.string A string in the form of a detailed message explaining the status of a backup index associated with the recovery point.
---@field EncryptionKeyType? aws.backup.EncryptionKeyType The type of encryption key used for the recovery point. Valid values are CUSTOMER_MANAGED_KMS_KEY for customer-managed keys or Amazon Web Services_OWNED_KMS_KEY for Amazon Web Services-owned keys.
---@field AggregatedScanResult? aws.backup.AggregatedScanResult Contains the latest scanning results against the recovery point and currently include FailedScan, Findings, LastComputed.

