---@class aws.backup.StartBackupJobInput
---@field BackupVaultName aws.backup.BackupVaultName The name of a logical container where backups are stored. Backup vaults are identified by names that are unique to the account used to create them and the Amazon Web Services Region where they are created.
---@field LogicallyAirGappedBackupVaultArn? aws.backup.ARN The ARN of a logically air-gapped vault. ARN must be in the same account and Region. If provided, supported fully managed resources back up directly to logically air-gapped vault, while other supported resources create a temporary (billable) snapshot in backup vault, then copy it to logically air-gapped vault. Unsupported resources only back up to the specified backup vault.
---@field ResourceArn aws.backup.ARN An Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that uniquely identifies a resource. The format of the ARN depends on the resource type.
---@field IamRoleArn aws.backup.IAMRoleArn Specifies the IAM role ARN used to create the target recovery point; for example, arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/S3Access.
---@field IdempotencyToken? aws.backup.string A customer-chosen string that you can use to distinguish between otherwise identical calls to StartBackupJob. Retrying a successful request with the same idempotency token results in a success message with no action taken.
---@field StartWindowMinutes? aws.backup.WindowMinutes A value in minutes after a backup is scheduled before a job will be canceled if it doesn't start successfully. This value is optional, and the default is 8 hours. If this value is included, it must be at least 60 minutes to avoid errors.
---@field CompleteWindowMinutes? aws.backup.WindowMinutes A value in minutes during which a successfully started backup must complete, or else Backup will cancel the job. This value is optional. This value begins counting down from when the backup was scheduled. It does not add additional time for StartWindowMinutes, or if the backup started later than scheduled.
---@field Lifecycle? aws.backup.Lifecycle The lifecycle defines when a protected resource is transitioned to cold storage and when it expires. Backup will transition and expire backups automatically according to the lifecycle that you define.
---@field RecoveryPointTags? aws.backup.Tags|distilled.Secret The tags to assign to the resources.
---@field BackupOptions? aws.backup.BackupOptions The backup option for a selected resource. This option is only available for Windows Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS) backup jobs.
---@field Index? aws.backup.Index|string Include this parameter to enable index creation if your backup job has a resource type that supports backup indexes.

